{
  "id": "ops_pdf_mail_012__long__cond",
  "snapshot": "thunderbird",
  "instruction": "On the Desktop, the folder \"to_send/\" contains two files: a spreadsheet \"mail_info.xlsx\" with the recipient / subject / body of the email, and an attachment source file. Convert the attachment source file into a PDF (saved next to it in the same folder, using the same base name), then open Thunderbird and send a new email exactly as described in \"mail_info.xlsx\", with the PDF attached.\n\nThunderbird is already configured; sending is captured locally, so you do not need real network access.",
  "source": "authors",
  "config": [
